# scripts/opcount: `jobsbench bench memory N` runs N jobs through a std
# jobs/memory queue, each enqueued, reserved and acked, with 64 waiting
# (ST2); the cost of one job is the slope between the two sizes. The
# control is hand Go with a heap of ready jobs and a map of leases under a
# mutex; the floor is a ring of ready jobs and a ring of lease ends.
unit job
sizes 200000 1200000
args bench memory {n}
control benchmarks/jobs/testdata/control
floor benchmarks/jobs/testdata/floor
